4
00:00:23.178 --> 00:00:45.089
healthcare. Please welcome the one and only Lady with the Lamp—Florence Nightingale!

5
00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.848
FLORENCE NIGHTINGALE: Thank

6
00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:51.311
you, Faye! FAYE MOSS: We can't wait to hear all about

7
00:00:51.312 --> 00:00:55.055
your career, Florence. Did you always dream about

8
00:00:55.056 --> 00:01:01.408
being a nurse? FLORENCE NIGHTINGALE: Well, as a child, I did enjoy taking care of family pets

9
00:01:01.409 --> 00:01:11.426
when they were injured. I was also intrigued by my relatives' ailments and kept a written record of things like my sister's toothache and an

10
00:01:11.427 --> 00:01:19.477
uncle's back pain! However, when I was born in 1820, females in Great Britain didn't think much

11
00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:26.050
about careers. Unless a woman was poor, she was just expected to get married and raise a

12
00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.114
family. FAYE MOSS: Did you go

13
00:01:28.115 --> 00:01:35.396
to school? FLORENCE NIGHTINGALE: No, but my family was quite wealthy, so my sister and I had a governess who

14
00:01:35.397 --> 00:01:42.611
gave us lessons. And my father tutored us in challenging subjects like physics,

15
00:01:42.612 --> 00:01:52.351
Greek, and statistics. In our household we were constantly discussing important issues, so I grew up yearning to do something meaningful with

16
00:01:52.352 --> 00:01:58.338
my life. At age 16, I had a religious awakening that affirmed this

17
00:01:58.339 --> 00:01:59.810
desire. FAYE MOSS: What

18
00:01:59.811 --> 00:02:06.095
do you mean? FLORENCE NIGHTINGALE: I had a strong feeling that God was calling on me

19
00:02:06.096 --> 00:02:10.687
to reduce human suffering. I eventually came to believe this meant

20
00:02:10.688 --> 00:02:13.977
becoming a nurse. FAYE MOSS: I bet your

21
00:02:13.978 --> 00:02:17.761
parents were proud of you! FLORENCE NIGHTINGALE:

22
00:02:17.762 --> 00:02:23.731
Quite the opposite, Faye—they were horrified! At the time most hospitals were filthy places

23
00:02:23.732 --> 00:02:31.300
where the poor went for treatment. Nurses were like servants who performed menial tasks such as emptying

24
